  "ai_language_tip": "Open in Ukrainian (uk); service in Ukrainian is the legal default for businesses. Many people also understand Russian, but do not switch unless the other side does; English works mainly in Kyiv/Lviv central venues and international hotels.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Younger staff in Kyiv, Lviv and Odesa city centres and hotels often manage; clinics, repair shops and state offices mostly Ukrainian only.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'Ви'; open with 'Добрий день' and say on whose behalf you call; first name + patronymic for older staff; close with 'Дякую, до побачення'. Direct and practical.",
  "name_tip": "Booking 'на прізвище …' (surname); many surnames are not gendered (-енко, -ук) but some are (-ський/-ська); spell Latin names letter by letter, expect Cyrillic transcription.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 0XX XXX XX XX (10 digits with 0, e.g. 067 12345678), international +380; confirmations by SMS, Viber or Telegram.",
  "time_tip": "24-hour in writing; speech 'о пів на восьму' = 7:30 (half TO eight) and 'за п'ятнадцять восьма' = 7:45; always read back in 24h ('о дев'ятнадцятій тридцять').",
  "number_tip": "Phone numbers are read in 3-3-2-2 groups (operator code, then hundreds, then two pairs) as whole numbers, so read back group by group; collective numerals for people ('нас троє', 'на двох').",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid restaurant peaks 13:00 and 19:00–21:00, calls after 21:00, and periods of air-raid alerts when staff may be in shelters; curfew hours vary by city under martial law.",
  "closed_days": "Most shops, restaurants and salons open 7 days; state offices close weekends; under martial law most public holidays are not days off, so business mostly continues.",
  "booking_channels": "Helsi (and similar e-health apps) for doctors; Expirenza and venue websites/Instagram for restaurant tables; Glovo and Bolt Food for delivery; Nova Poshta app for parcels; phone, Viber and Telegram dominant for small businesses; Diia for state services.",
  "voice_menu": "Mobile operators (Kyivstar, Vodafone, lifecell), banks, Nova Poshta and utilities use IVR or chat bots; small venues answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Clinics send SMS/Helsi reminders; small businesses confirm in Viber/Telegram; restaurants may call back on the day for big tables.",
